WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.601
-You know our next guest
for his work on

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.901
"Gossip Girl" and "Easy A."

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:05.634
He returns to star in
the fourth season of "You."

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:07.167
Part 1 begins
streaming globally

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:08.467
on Netflix February 9th.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:09.701
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:13.033
-Whose coat is this?

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.100
-Easy does it.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.667
Time to get this one home.

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:19.334
Couch, couch, couch.

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:22.868
-Malcolm got me home.

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.968
Do I need to thank him? No.

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:27.968
If I'm rude, maybe the
misogynist with a drug problem

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:29.033
will leave me alone.

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:33.167
New day.

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:35.000
No more craziness.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.234
Back to the quiet.

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:39.434
[ Ominous music plays ]

00:00:39.434 --> 00:00:42.367
-Please welcome to the show,
Penn Badgley, everybody!

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:45.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.367
♪♪

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:55.767
♪♪

00:00:55.767 --> 00:01:01.200
♪♪

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.267
I'm so happy to have you here!

00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:03.634
-Yo!

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:05.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:08.734
Alright, I think this is
the first studio audience

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:11.067
since like, 2020, since COVID.

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:14.300
-Is it jarring to be back in
front of human beings like this?

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.868
-I mean, well, like this,
it's always jarring.

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:18.234
-Right, right, yeah.

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:19.567
-It's not --

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:20.767
-It's not a natural
state of things.

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:23.634
-Yeah, it's nothing on you.
All on me.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:26.767
-This is a show, as evidenced by
the reaction when you came out,

00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:28.334
with a very devoted fanbase,

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:30.300
but also, you play
a very terrible person.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.434
-Yeah.
-Is that confounding to you,

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:34.367
that this is where people
are like,

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:35.834
"We love watching Penn do this."

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:36.934
-I mean...

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:40.100
So, yes, I mean,
I somewhat famously played

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.701
a cultural ref back when
it first came out,

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:45.868
and I was like, you know,
"He's a murderer!"

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:50.133
But I think now I'm just like,
that's also on us a bit.

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:52.000
We designed him.
-We're drawn to it.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.667
-We designed him that way.

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:54.901
But it's, yeah, man.

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:56.334
I feel like I have
a front row seat

00:01:56.334 --> 00:02:00.534
to this particular kind of...

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:02.667
that thing, you know?

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:06.734
The obsession thing,
and so, you know,

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:08.067
I bear witness and it's cool.

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:10.767
-There's some pretty gnarly
scenes in the show.

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:14.267
I would imagine it gets pretty
gross with the special effects.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.400
-Yeah.
-Are there times where

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.968
you have to take a minute?

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:19.334
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:24.300
I'm not precious about
my process in any way,

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:28.334
but there have been a few times
where I've spontaneously

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.367
become nauseous.

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:33.801
Just in this last season --

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:37.200
when you don't finish a scene
on time in the day,

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.400
you have to go back
and do pick-ups,

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.834
and so I was in the middle
of something else.

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:41.400
I'm like, "Yeah, we're gonna go
do pick-ups for this scene

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.100
from the second episode
or first episode.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.234
Sure, yeah, yeah."

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:46.868
And then I got to strap on
this jumpsuit,

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.534
and then I'm like, "Oh, right."

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.400
And then they spray me down
with blood, like,

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.801
fully, fully.

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:53.667
I have goggles on
and I'm just like,

00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:55.000
"Okay, alright."

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.567
And then I walk into
this room they've created

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:00.400
to make it look like the place
we were in,

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.534
and it's full of smoke
and dark, fake blood

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:08.968
all over a table,
and a table saw with meat on it.

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:10.334
[ Crowd groans ]

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:11.801
-Yeah, that's -- yeah.

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:15.901
And, um, and I remember just
being like -- [Shudders]

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:18.167
It's not, um --

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:21.334
Your nervous system is
just like, "No!"

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.400
-Yeah, right.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.067
And I would imagine, too,
when you're like,

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:25.801
"Alright, now what's this
character thinking?"

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:27.501
that's not a nice place
to go, either.

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:30.767
-Well, you know what's nice
is that

00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:33.434
he's meant to be --

00:03:33.434 --> 00:03:36.734
he's your likeable
serial killer.

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:38.534
He's your clumsy, like,
killer next door.

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:41.534
-He's a little, bumbling --

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:43.567
-So I just let the nausea
come through.

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:47.868
-Now, obviously, this was

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:50.100
a highly anticipated season,

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.934
and this was the art that you
put on social media.

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:56.467
But I've heard -- well,
you actually shared

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:57.801
after you posted it.
-I did.

00:03:57.801 --> 00:04:00.434
-You had posted it maybe
before you were allowed.

00:04:00.434 --> 00:04:02.868
-Yeah, before the embargo
was lifted.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:05.667
Which makes it feel like
I'm an ambassador or something.

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:07.667
Like, "embargo."
-But a Netflix embargo,

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:08.868
I would imagine
that's a real deal.

00:04:08.868 --> 00:04:10.067
-It is, yeah.

00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:13.067
To be honest, I don't post much
on social media.

00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:16.400
My batting average is high,
but I do not actually post.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.834
I do not actually
post that much.

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:20.100
-It's very good to wait for
a big announcement like that.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.234
-And even there had been
bigger announcements

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:23.767
about this season.

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:25.000
I hadn't posted.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:25.968
But I just thought,
"You know what?

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:27.300
I'll do it this morning."

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.200
And I had a lot to do with my
son, and I was just like,

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.567
"If I don't do it now,
I'm not gonna do it."

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:31.968
It was 9:00 in the morning.

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:34.501
And I went to this, like,

00:04:34.501 --> 00:04:36.334
there's this secret spreadsheet
from Netflix.

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:37.634
It's very confidential.

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:41.434
It made me quite nervous,
actually,

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:45.267
and I second-guessed it,
but then I found it.

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:47.534
It was all very complicated.
And I posted.

00:04:47.534 --> 00:04:49.901
-As a fellow performer,

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:52.000
if I look at a spreadsheet,
I also get very nervous.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.334
-Yeah, it's just --

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:55.033
-A lot of
the spreadsheet stuff in school

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:56.701
was not my forte.

00:04:56.701 --> 00:05:00.234
-But I posted,

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:02.467
And I'm posting it on Instagram
and I'm thinking,

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:04.200
"What's a cute caption?

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.767
'Felt cute might delete.'"

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:08.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:10.501
And I felt cute about that.

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:13.067
-You were being honest.

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:14.367
-Yeah, no. I felt cute,

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:16.200
and I had no intention
of deleting it.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.367
-Yeah.

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:18.634
-And then I go back
to the spreadsheet --

00:05:18.634 --> 00:05:20.000
why, I don't know --

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.133
and it says,

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:25.934
"Do not post until noon."

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:27.567
And I was like...

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:29.901
I mean, it's 9:00.

00:05:29.901 --> 00:05:31.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:34.701
Is that a big deal? Three hours?

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.634
Like, does that matter?

00:05:36.634 --> 00:05:37.601
And I'm thinking to myself,
like,

00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:41.133
"Okay, who cares? Should I?"

00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:43.734
But then I was like,
"No, I'm gonna..."

00:05:43.734 --> 00:05:46.300
And I deleted it,
and then I realized...

00:05:48.701 --> 00:05:50.167
...I felt cute and I deleted it.

00:05:50.167 --> 00:05:51.234
-Yeah!

00:05:51.234 --> 00:05:53.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.634 --> 00:05:55.601
-And then -- no, and then --

00:05:55.601 --> 00:05:57.133
So at this point,
the post doesn't exist

00:05:57.133 --> 00:05:59.200
except to the few, I don't know,

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.467
100 or maybe 1,000 people
who saw it,

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:02.467
and I thought,

00:06:02.467 --> 00:06:04.400
"That was brilliant."

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:05.467
-Yeah!

00:06:05.467 --> 00:06:07.334
-To them, the few!

00:06:07.334 --> 00:06:11.367
And then I thought,
"Do I leave it like that

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:14.634
or do I follow through
and post the post

00:06:14.634 --> 00:06:17.434
that I was gonna post because
I'm trying to be a team player?"

00:06:17.434 --> 00:06:19.434
And so then I posted it,
and believe it or not,

00:06:19.434 --> 00:06:21.801
I posted all of this
in a caption.

00:06:21.801 --> 00:06:24.400
-Yeah.
What you just told us.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.634
-I might have told the story
better in that caption.

00:06:26.634 --> 00:06:27.901
So you can go check.

00:06:27.901 --> 00:06:31.334
-You know, if your phone
has the megabytes

00:06:31.334 --> 00:06:32.968
to download the whole post.

00:06:32.968 --> 00:06:35.033
It's a really cool show.

00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:36.334
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:06:36.334 --> 00:06:37.200
We really appreciate it.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.501
You guys, that's Penn Badgley!

00:06:38.501 --> 00:06:40.968
The first part of
Season 4 of "You"

00:06:40.968 --> 00:06:42.434
begins streaming today
on Netflix.

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:43.634
We'll be right back
with "Late Night."

